WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:00.894
CMMC 2.

00:00:00.894 --> 00:00:05.261
0 uses three levels: Level 1, Level 2, and Level 3.

00:00:05.261 --> 00:00:11.216
The levels connect information sensitivity and contract risk to increasingly rigorous cybersecurity and verification expectations.

00:00:11.216 --> 00:00:13.201
Level 1 is called Foundational.

00:00:13.201 --> 00:00:17.966
It focuses on basic safeguarding requirements associated with Federal Contract Information and

00:00:17.966 --> 00:00:22.333
is based on the requirements in the federal contract safeguarding clause.

00:00:22.333 --> 00:00:26.700
Level 1 uses self-assessment and affirmation mechanisms under the CMMC program.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:30.273
It is not a promise that risk has disappeared;

00:00:30.273 --> 00:00:35.434
the organization is representing that required practices are implemented within the applicable scope.

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:37.419
Level 2 is called Advanced.

00:00:37.419 --> 00:00:42.183
It aligns with the 110 security requirements in NIST SP 800-171 Revision

00:00:42.183 --> 00:00:45.756
2 for protecting CUI in nonfederal systems and organizations.

00:00:45.756 --> 00:00:48.139
Depending on the acquisition and contract,

00:00:48.139 --> 00:00:52.903
Level 2 may involve either a self-assessment or an assessment by an

00:00:52.903 --> 00:00:54.888
authorized CMMC Third-Party Assessment Organization.

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:58.064
The solicitation and contract identify the required status.

00:00:58.064 --> 00:01:00.049
Level 3 is called Expert.

00:01:00.049 --> 00:01:04.813
It builds on Level 2 and adds selected requirements associated with NIST

00:01:04.813 --> 00:01:09.577
SP 800-172 for environments supporting higher-priority CUI and facing more advanced risk.

00:01:09.577 --> 00:01:14.738
Level 3 assessment involves the government assessment function defined by the CMMC program.

00:01:14.738 --> 00:01:19.502
An organization pursuing Level 3 must also satisfy the underlying Level 2

00:01:19.502 --> 00:01:21.488
expectations for the applicable scope.

00:01:21.488 --> 00:01:27.443
The practical lesson is not to choose a level based on preference or marketing language.

00:01:27.443 --> 00:01:32.207
Organizations should use current official requirements and the applicable solicitation or contract

00:01:32.207 --> 00:01:34.192
to determine the required level,

00:01:34.192 --> 00:01:35.780
assessment type, and timing.
